%
% paper/references.bib (the verified bibliography, Anthology-id keys) holds every entry whose
% identifier was confirmed; THIS file holds only the entries it lacks (grammars, resources, a blog,
% statistics classics, model reports, patching methods), so that the manuscript compiles. On 1 October 2026
% ten entries (XCOPA, SentencePiece, BPE, Rust et al., Ahia et al., Pham & Pham, Phun-Bench, KoWit-24,
% Kaushal & Mahowald, Itzhak & Levy) were verified against the Anthology XML and moved to references.bib. Entries were
% drafted from the founding plan's source list (docs/PLAN_2026-09-30.md) and from memory;
% author lists, titles, venues, pages and identifiers may be wrong or incomplete. ACL 2026
% desk-rejected over 100 accepted papers for citing non-existent literature: every entry
% must be confirmed by hand against the ACL Anthology / arXiv / publisher page and recorded
% in docs/RELATED_WORK_VERIFICATION.md before it is cited in a submitted PDF. references.bib
% has landed and main.tex cites both files; this file shrinks as entries are verified and moved
% there, and is deleted when it is empty. tests/test_paper.py refuses a key present in both files.
%
% Conventions: Anthology-style keys (surname-etal-year-firstword); Unicode is avoided
% (BibTeX); each entry carries note = {UNVERIFIED}. Vietnamese letters use the T5 (vntex)
% accent macros: a tone accent over a quality-marked letter is written {\'{\^e}} (\^e = e-circumflex),
% {\d{\^e}}, {\~{\uhorn}} (\uhorn = u-horn), {\`{\^o}}; tests/test_paper.py re-renders every macro to
% NFC and compares the Vietnamese fields with the intended strings. Checked at the first pdflatex build (1 October 2026, TeX Live 2023 vntex): the unbraced stacked
% form {\'\^e} FAILS ("You can't use a prefix with `end-group character'"); the braced form {\'{\^e}} compiles,
% so every stacked accent here braces its base.
% =====================================================================

